{"title":"Cube (geometry)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>cube</b>, or regular <b>hexahedron</b>, is a solid composed of six <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_(geometry)\" title=\"Square (geometry)\"> square</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Face\" title=\"Face\">faces</a>. A cube is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Platonic_solid#Duality\" title=\"Platonic solid\"> dual</a> to the regular <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Octahedron\" title=\"Octahedron\">octahedron</a> and has <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Octahedral_symmetry&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Octahedral symmetry (page does not exist)\">octahedral symmetry</a>. A cube is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Platonic_solid\" title=\"Platonic solid\">Platonic solid</a>. All edges of cubes are equal to each other.\n</p><p>The cube is also a square <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelepiped\" title=\"Parallelepiped\">parallelepiped</a>, an equilateral cuboid, and a right rhombohedron a 3-zonohedron. It is a regular square prism in three orientations, and a trigonal trapezohedron in four orientations. \n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Formulas\">Formulas</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Formulas\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A cube with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edge</a>-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">length</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> has:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Four space <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonals</a> of same lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283ce2359a61e0c21fb3c59fc839774494da9dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/0/8a0d43bc2f4c1a417da3ab5e9bdfc47a94455e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{s^2+s^2+s^2}=\\sqrt{3s^2}=s\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"19\" />)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Surface_area\" title=\"Surface area\">Surface area</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80ba0603c463273e2fa2ac1b1bfef84d3f02cc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" />. (6 sides of areas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764ebc651e88ea62ad69ae4b4a7ffdc839c64468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\cdot s$\" width=\"29\" height=\"8\" />.)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Volume\" title=\"Volume\">Volume</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1efd9b312e1b222638097dc259b25af7a72779d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^3$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b4544e719df4d97a5ea69df14f15214e2e02cbec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\cdot s \\cdot s$\" width=\"51\" height=\"8\" />)</li>\n<li>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumscribe\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Circumscribe\">circumscribed</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sphere\" title=\"Sphere\">sphere</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/8/de81b5461afbe619986fc6a7446efe044f37cd04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" /></li>\n<li>An <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inscribe\" title=\"Inscribe\">inscribed</a> sphere of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c5372e4a6aa030c5c2973cc7aad79bad38f9241b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" /></li>\n<li>A sphere <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to all of its edges of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69236867c2e19e51ad90b7e34350702b471948c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{s\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" /></li>\n<li>A regular tetrahedron can fit in exactly two ways inside a cube</li></ul>\n<ul><li>For any cube whose circumscribing sphere has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and for any given point in the its 3D dimensional space with distances <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> from the cube's eight vertices, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/9/c690a5a8732c460805c5e0bc569e364904e1a785.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{8} d_i^2}{8} + \\frac{16R^4}{9} = (\\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{8} d_i^2}{8}+\\frac{2R^2}{3})^2.\\]\" width=\"300\" height=\"42\" /></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube_(geometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hexahedron\" title=\"Hexahedron\">Hexahedron</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prism\" title=\"Prism\">Prism</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Cube_(geometry)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017214410\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 94/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2346/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.756      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.756      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4021:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017214410 and revision id 192475. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}